# Sonnet Worker Delegation — Iteration 5

## Task
041-inbox-linked-payment-account — lifecycle clearing bug fixes

## Context
Codex review-3.md found two bugs in `updateAccount` lifecycle clearing (both introduced
by task 041 P6). No other file needs to change.

## Approved Fixes

### Fix 1 (High) — line ~575: dependent-link clearing condition is too narrow
Current code:
```ts
if (archiving || typeChangingAwayFromCreditCard) {
  await tx
    .update(accounts)
    .set({ linkedAccountId: null })
    .where(and(eq(accounts.linkedAccountId, id), eq(accounts.userId, userId)));
}
```
When a payer account changes type FROM `bank` TO `credit_card`, `typeChangingAwayFromCreditCard`
is false (that variable tracks the EDITED account's own old type being credit_card).
So credit cards that had this account as their payer keep pointing to it — now illegally linked
to another credit card.

Change the condition to:
```ts
if (archiving || (typeChanged && nextType === "credit_card")) {
```

Explanation: the dependent accounts must have their link cleared whenever the edited account
becomes ineligible as a payer. An account is ineligible when it is archived OR when its type
becomes credit_card (credit cards cannot be payers).

### Fix 2 (Medium) — line ~566: archiving a credit card doesn't clear its own link
Current spread inside the main `set()`:
```ts
...(typeChangingAwayFromCreditCard ? { linkedAccountId: null } : {}),
```
When a credit card is archived, `typeChangingAwayFromCreditCard` is false, so its
`linkedAccountId` is never cleared.

Change to clear the edited account's own link when it is a credit card being archived OR
changing away from credit_card type:
```ts
...((typeChangingAwayFromCreditCard || (archiving && current.type === "credit_card")) ? { linkedAccountId: null } : {}),
```

