- `apps/api/src/modules/ledger/services/accounts.ts`
  - function `updateAccount` (the exported wrapper that calls `withTransaction`)
  - variable `typeChangingAwayFromCreditCard` (line ~395) — no change needed to this variable
  - main `set()` call spread (line ~566)
  - lifecycle `if` block after the update (line ~575)

## Must Not Change
- `typeChangingAwayFromCreditCard` variable definition — it is still used for the own-link clear
- any other file in the repository

## Acceptance Criteria
- AC-F1: When account X (bank/non-CC) changes type to credit_card, any credit cards that
  had `linkedAccountId = X.id` now have `linkedAccountId = null`
- AC-F2: When a credit card is archived, its own `linkedAccountId` is cleared to null in
  the same `UPDATE` that sets `archivedAt`
- AC-F3: Existing behaviour — archiving a bank account clears dependent cards' links —
  is preserved
- AC-F4: Existing behaviour — changing a CC type away from credit_card clears its own link
  and clears dependent cards that had it as payer — is preserved
- AC-F5: `npm run typecheck` exits 0

## Commands
1. Apply both edits to `apps/api/src/modules/ledger/services/accounts.ts`
2. Run `npm run typecheck` and capture full output + exit code

